														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2008741">
									

<p>The classic Thing that does a Thing SCP is basically that it does X under Y circumstances, with little other information not directly related to that or its containment procedure.</p>
<p>This thing either becomes a Dragon or Oni, and requires a special task force to defeat it while dressed as either Knights or Samurai, or it goes on a rampage. It has no testing logs, no interview, no associated tales, no [REDACTED] or [DATA EXPUNGED], no interface screw, no horrible implications written between the lines&#8230; it just does X under Y circumstances, and we're given all the information needed to understand what it does and why it needs the Special Containment Procedures.</p>
<p>That's why I call it a classic Thing that does a Thing SCP. Of course, that's just my opinion of what makes a classic Thing that does a Thing SCP.</p>

