<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Uh.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Uh.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>So… what if one day SCP-2301 got tired of the usual medieval fantasy stuff and decides to do sci-fi instead? Now what would the Foundation do?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why, hire Tom Cruise, of course.</p>
<p><em>But he might die!</em></p>
<p>Might he, now&#8230; ? /sly smile</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Without reliance on other skips, the task force personnel would need to improvise with current laser and walker tech and stuff like that, or they could get lucky if normal guns are sufficient to stop SCP-2301 which would made the whole thing easier to contain than with katanas, though those guns would have to be modified to look like typical sci fi video game guns to work. Or they could use 'futuristic' drones armed with lasers.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Depending on the version of the story, which might become a tough problem here. That is&#8230; is SCP-2301 representing a Star Trek-type fantasy, where a yellow or blue suit may solve the problem but a red one is an almost certain death warrant? Or is it representing a Star Wars-type story, where it will be beaten by Ewan McGregor with a beard and a glowing stick? Or a Farscape story? Or a Galactica story? Or a DC/Marvel one? Or a bloody Angel from NGE? Would we need an EVA in that last scenario? To us, it might be obvious. To a researcher, and to the guys waiting there with armors and swords, it would not.</p>
<p>Let's just say that making it stick to stereotypical &quot;traditional&quot; settings might be easier to sort out. I wonder what was it doing before entering containment, though&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A lulz ending can also be used in which SCP-2301 appears as a monster that can be defeated with normal modern military weapons like nukes and the like. A Foundation researcher will also make the suggestion to decrease the class level down to safe if the skip decides to stay modern indefinitely.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230; having to use nukes to contain a thing that can become whatever it &quot;wants&quot; does not sound like a safe-class skip.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyways, sorry. Liked it, Weizhong. This makes my fun sense tingle. : D</p>

							</div>

								
					
